---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/compare/sequenzy-vs-shopify-email";
const title = "Sequenzy vs Shopify Email for Shopify: 2026 Decision Guide";
const desc = "Audit native automations before migrating. A scoped Shopify workflow comparison with current product evidence and proposed acceptance checks.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does Shopify support automated welcome and recovery email?",
    "answer": "Yes. Current Shopify Messaging documentation covers marketing automations triggered by signup and abandonment. Audit those before deciding to migrate."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is an abandoned cart the same as an abandoned checkout?",
    "answer": "No. Define whether the shopper added products or began checkout, then inspect the corresponding trigger, identity and channel eligibility."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must I move at a particular order count?",
    "answer": "No. Move for a demonstrated workflow or operating need. Volume alone does not prove that native automation is inadequate."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I cost native recovery?",
    "answer": "Shopify documents abandoned-checkout email automation as excluded from email-send totals. Separate it from other counted sends when modeling the bill."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep Shopify newsletters during evaluation?",
    "answer": "Yes as an operating choice, but document audiences and exclusions across campaigns and flows so the same customer is not unintentionally contacted twice."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should remain in Shopify?",
    "answer": "Retain the transactional notifications and workflows you intend Shopify to own. Inventory responsibilities explicitly rather than treating email migration as replacement of every notification."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="badge">Shopify decision guide</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sequenzy vs Shopify Email</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">A Shopify merchant considering Sequenzy should first inventory what already runs in Shopify. Current help calls the app Shopify Messaging and documents automated marketing, not just manual newsletters. The decision is whether a specific missing workflow or operating requirement warrants another platform.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>What Shopify already offers</h2>
      <p>Shopify documents marketing automations for signup and abandonment, with custom workflows available through Shopify Flow. Its current help distinguishes abandoned browse, cart and checkout. Sequenzy documents a visual builder, commerce flows and API/agent access. A fair evaluation starts with the actual native workflow, not an assumption that Shopify cannot send a triggered welcome or recovery email.</p>
      <h2>Separate cart from checkout</h2>
      <p>A shopper viewing a product, adding it to a cart and starting checkout has crossed different event boundaries. Before migrating recovery, write which stage you intend to target and what identity is available there. Shopify documents channel restrictions for abandoned-checkout automation. Inspect the sales channel and recipient eligibility of an example checkout before declaring an absent email a platform failure.</p>
      <h2>Proposed trial: candle care after purchase</h2>
      <p>For a hypothetical candle shop, request a care email after the relevant fulfillment and suppress promotional follow-up on cancellation. Inventory the native workflow and the available fulfillment data, then reproduce the same conditions in Sequenzy. Use a split fulfillment and a cancelled order as counterexamples. The test is whether the right order causes one appropriate message, not whether a builder has a template named post-purchase. No merchant outcomes are claimed here.</p>
      <h2>Custom properties need a producer</h2>
      <p>If gift buyers should receive different content, identify where the gift indication originates: an order attribute, line item or another app. Do not assume either platform infers it. Map its type and scope, including a mixed gift-and-self order. If a custom bridge is required, cost its implementation and support. A profile tag is convenient but can be wrong when the same shopper places different kinds of orders.</p>
      <h2>Explain the reason for every skipped send</h2>
      <p>Shopify help documents situations in which abandoned-checkout mail is not delivered, including a completed purchase and items no longer available. Inspect recent automation activity before rebuilding the journey elsewhere. In a Sequenzy evaluation, require equivalent visibility into event arrival, eligibility and purchase exits. Distinguish a missing event from a deliberate exclusion: they require different fixes.</p>
      <h2>Count the correct billable messages</h2>
      <p>Shopify documents that abandoned-checkout email automations are excluded from monthly email-send totals, while other email automations count. Sequenzy advertises email-send plans with unlimited contacts. Build the comparison from eligible campaigns and automation sends, excluding native checkout sends where applicable. Add operator hours, integration work and seasonal volume. Do not equate attributed recovery revenue with revenue a migration would add.</p>
      <h2>A reversible workflow cutover</h2>
      <p>List native automations, Flow workflows and third-party senders before switching anything. Choose one workflow, authenticate the new sender, compare links and exclusions, then stop the old enrollment point before activating the replacement. Decide explicitly how waiting contacts finish. Keep purchase receipts and other transactional responsibilities on their intended system; marketing migration does not require moving every Shopify notification.</p>
      <h2>When staying is the better decision</h2>
      <p>Stay with Shopify Messaging when its native and Flow workflows express your needs and the team can operate them. Evaluate Sequenzy when agent access, a separate email workspace or a demonstrated workflow gap solves a real problem. Ask the regular operator to explain and edit the candle-care exclusions in each. There is no defensible universal order count, revenue percentage or store age at which every merchant must graduate.</p>
      <h2>Sources and evaluation limits</h2>
      <p>Supplier documentation checked November 24, 2026. These are documented capabilities and proposed decision checks, not firsthand product tests or measured merchant results. Account eligibility, payloads and current quotes need confirmation before activation.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/shopify-messaging/marketing-automations">Shopify marketing automations</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/migrate-abandoned-checkout">Shopify checkout migration and exclusions</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/shopify-messaging/marketing-automations/requirements-considerations">Shopify automation pricing considerations</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">Sequenzy builder and commerce features</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-omnisend">Sequenzy vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-mailchimp">Sequenzy vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/print-on-demand">Email apps for print-on-demand</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Sequenzy vs Shopify Email FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
